> SCAPS Material parameters file, saved on 	13-11-2013 at 19:01:04
> 
> Silicon parameters from Sze, Physics of Semiconductor devices, 2dn ed., 1981
> But for:
> Effective masses: average between "density of states effective mass" and "effective mass for Richardson constant" (both taken from Sze)
> Thermal velocities from the website of Ioffe Institute, Russia
> Radiative and Auger recombination from Tyagi, Introduction to semiconductor materials and devices, 1991
> SRH recombination: single level assumed mid-gap, sigma_n and p, Nt set to obtain Ln and Lp around 100 micrometer
> Optical absorption from file distributed with SCAPS
> No doping type nor extrinsic doping is set! (NA = ND = 1E10/cm3 = about ni)
> 
> Should be OK for low doped silicon. For higher doping, the mobilities should be set to an appropriate lower value; the recombination then should adapt itself
> 
